<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<odoo>
    <!--
      The Sales dashboard, rewritten: same entry, same place in the sidebar.

      The core record (spreadsheet_dashboard_sale.spreadsheet_dashboard_sales)
      keeps its name, group and sequence; only its content changes. Two
      clocks, one under the other: the order by order date, the fiscal note
      by note date — and the core's own tables (top quotations, top orders,
      top customers, top teams) below them, rebuilt in the same sheet so one
      period filter moves everything.

      Why rewrite rather than add a second dashboard: the owner did not want
      a second "Sales" in the sidebar (05/09/2026), and a dashboard named
      differently was the first attempt — "Sales vs. notes" — retired on
      06/09/2026 once its content moved here.

      If spreadsheet_dashboard_sale is ever updated on its own, its data file
      puts the core content back; a `-u` of this module restores ours.
    -->
    <record id="spreadsheet_dashboard_sale.spreadsheet_dashboard_sales" model="spreadsheet.dashboard">
        <field name="spreadsheet_binary_data" type="base64"
               file="liber_sales_dashboard/data/files/sales_dashboard.json"/>
        <field name="main_data_model_ids"
               eval="[Command.link(ref('sale.model_sale_order')),
                      Command.link(ref('liber_nfe_xml.model_nfe_xml_panel'))]"/>
    </record>
</odoo>
